  "summary": "Malicious code in beaver-ui-form (npm)",
  "details": "The package pretends to be a UI form component but its postinstall hook (node setup.js) downloads and executes platform-specific binaries. It fingerprints the operating system and architecture, then downloads a binary from Cloudflare Workers subdomains (oob-worker[.]cf) or via DNS TXT records from well1[.]site. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e on Linux/macOS or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows, then launched as a detached background process. The package also attempts to load the same dropper when imported via require(). A large decoy telemetry.js file pads the package to appear legitimate.",
  "affected": [
